.TH PATH_DIRNAME_B 3
.SH NAME
path_dirname_b \- extract the directory component of a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "char* path_dirname_b(const char* " path ", size_t " size ", stralloc* " dir ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_dirname_b
extracts the directory portion of the path provided in the buffer
.I path
of length
.IR size ,
storing the result in the
.B stralloc
structure pointed to by
.IR dir .
.PP
The function follows standard directory parsing logic:
.IP \(bu
If the path contains a directory component, it is returned minus the final path separator(s) and basename.
.IP \(bu
If the path does not contain a directory component, or represents a single component, the current directory (".") is returned.
.IP \(bu
Trailing path separators are ignored during the calculation of the directory length.
.PP
The resulting string in
.I dir
is null-terminated.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the null-terminated string buffer within the
.B stralloc
structure
.I dir
on success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_basename2 (3),
.BR path_dirlen_b (3),
.BR stralloc (3)